item.text:
**Reused evidence**
REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0001"],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.5"]}

**New evidence**
- Khamenei’s first 2022 public response to the protests framed them as foreign-backed “riots,” which is directly relevant to incitement and crisis response.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran’s Khamenei blames Israel, US in first comments on protests","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-10-03","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/news/2022/10/3/irans-khamenei-blames-israel-us-in-first-comments-on-protests","claim":"Khamenei called the anti-government protests 'riots' and blamed the United States and Israel for trying to stop Iran's progress.","locator":"article body, quoted speech to graduating police cadets","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct contemporaneous quotation and clear date, but mediated through a secondary publisher.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 protest period","ruler_attribution":"Direct attribution to Khamenei in his role as Supreme Leader.","contrary_evidence":["He also said Mahsa Amini's death 'deeply broke my heart,' which is a limited sympathetic note but not restraint.","The speech was accusatory rather than protective and did not acknowledge state responsibility."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Earlier in 2022, Khamenei used the same enemy-framing pattern against protests, reinforcing the incitement record rather than checking it.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Khamenei blames unrest on 'enemies' out to overthrow Islamic Republic","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-06-05","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/05/us-iran-khamenei-protests","claim":"Khamenei blamed protests on foreign 'enemies' seeking to overthrow the Islamic Republic and described them as psychological warfare against Iran.","locator":"opening paragraph and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting a direct quotation from Khamenei in the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 pre-protest-wave baseline","ruler_attribution":"Direct attribution to Khamenei.","contrary_evidence":["This was rhetoric about unrest, not a direct operational order.","The speech did not itself document killings or arrests."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.8","3B.10"]}
- The UN’s first immediate public response to Mahsa Amini’s death captures the trigger and the violent state response.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mahsa Amini: Acting UN human rights chief urges impartial probe into death in Iran","publisher":"OHCHR","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2022/09/mahsa-amini-acting-un-human-rights-chief-urges-impartial-probe-death-iran","claim":"The UN said Amini died after detention by Iran's morality police and reported violent security-force responses to ensuing protests, including live ammunition, injuries, arrests, and calls for an independent probe.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN human-rights statement issued days after the death, with direct contemporaneous reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 trigger event","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong attribution to the state apparatus under Khamenei's authority.","contrary_evidence":["It is an early UN statement, not a completed fact-finding report.","It records allegations and reports at a very early stage."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.7","3B.8","3B.9"]}
- The OHCHR communication on Iran’s protests is useful because it records the pattern of live fire, torture, executions, and internet disruption at the time.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Communication report: Iran (Islamic Republic of) IRN 23/2022","publisher":"OHCHR Special Procedures Communications","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://spcommreports.ohchr.org/TmSearch/SearchCode?code=IRN+23%2F2022%3B+IRN+11%2F2025%3B+IRN+30%2F2022","claim":"OHCHR recorded information concerning excessive and lethal force, live ammunition, arbitrary arrests, torture, extrajudicial executions, unlawful killings, and internet disruption in response to the Amini protests.","locator":"communication summary for IRN 23/2022","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN special-procedures communication summarizing a contemporaneous rights complaint.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 protest period","ruler_attribution":"State-aligned security conduct under Khamenei's top-level authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is a communication record, not a merits finding.","The page summarizes received allegations rather than a final adjudication."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.5","3B.8","3B.9"]}
- Network-measurement evidence shows the government used connectivity restrictions as part of the crackdown.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Internet disrupted in Iran amid protests over death of Mahsa Amini","publisher":"NetBlocks","publication_date":"2022-09-19","url":"https://netblocks.org/reports/internet-disrupted-in-iran-amid-protests-over-death-of-mahsa-amini-X8qVEwAD","claim":"NetBlocks confirmed near-total internet disruption in parts of Kurdistan province and later nationwide platform and mobile-network restrictions during the Amini protests.","locator":"posted report summary","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent network telemetry provider with contemporaneous measurements and clear protest linkage.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 protest onset and follow-on shutdowns","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Iranian authorities and their security councils, not a private Khamenei order transcript.","contrary_evidence":["Connectivity was temporarily restored in some places, so this was not a uniform all-country blackout at every moment.","The report measures disruption, not the legal authority behind each order."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9"]}
- Amnesty’s September 2022 report is one of the strongest contemporaneous accounts of lethal force against protesters, including children.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: World must take meaningful action against bloody crackdown as death toll rises","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/09/iran-world-must-take-meaningful-action-against-bloody-crackdown-as-death-toll-rises/","claim":"Amnesty said Iranian security forces were deliberately and unlawfully firing live ammunition at protesters, with at least 30 people killed, including four children, across multiple cities and provinces.","locator":"opening summary and live-ammunition paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous human-rights investigation with specific casualty and conduct claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 protest wave","ruler_attribution":"State security forces under Khamenei's authority; not a private speech transcript.","contrary_evidence":["The report is advocacy-based, so individual incidents need corroboration where possible.","It does not by itself establish every chain-of-command step."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.7","3B.8","3B.9"]}
- The Persian-language Human Rights Watch country chapter is a useful local-language summary of the 2022 crackdown and protest environment.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2023: ايران","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2023-01-12","url":"https://www.hrw.org/fa/world-report/2023/country-chapters/iran","claim":"HRW said Iranian security forces responded to widespread protests with excessive and lethal force, thousands were arrested, and authorities heavily disrupted internet access.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the Persian country chapter","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Persian-language HRW summary of the 2022 record; broad but consistent with other independent accounts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Year-end synthesis of the 2022 protest cycle","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong attribution to the Iranian state under Khamenei.","contrary_evidence":["This is a summary chapter rather than a case file.","It compresses many incidents into a broad overview."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- The first known protest-related execution is a clear due-process and intimidation marker.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Horrifying execution of young protester exposes authorities’ cruelty and risk of further bloodshed","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-12-08","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/12/iran-horrifying-execution-of-young-protester-exposes-authorities-cruelty-and-risk-of-further-bloodshed/","claim":"Amnesty said Iran executed Mohsen Shekari after a grossly unfair sham trial for participation in the protests, less than three weeks after conviction.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted Amnesty response","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights-reporting on a named execution with fair-trial critique.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-2022 escalation","ruler_attribution":"State judiciary action under the Supreme Leader's system; not a personal Khamenei transcript.","contrary_evidence":["Iran portrayed the case as punishment for violence against security forces.","The source is advocacy-based, though the execution itself was public and undisputed."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- The crackdown extended to children, and the authorities allegedly coerced families into silence.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Authorities covering up their crimes of child killings by coercing families into silence","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-12-09","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/12/iran-authorities-covering-up-their-crimes-of-child-killings-by-coercing-families-into-silence/","claim":"Amnesty documented at least 44 children killed by security forces in connection with the protests and said authorities harassed families to silence them and accept official narratives.","locator":"opening summary and family-harassment paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous documentation with named child-victim counts and family intimidation allegations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 protest period","ruler_attribution":"Security-force conduct and post-incident coercion under Khamenei's authority.","contrary_evidence":["The authority response is partly inferential because the report aggregates many incidents.","The report is not a court judgment."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- Schoolgirl poisonings began in late 2022 and the authorities were criticized for failing to investigate them adequately.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ایران – میلیون‌ها دختر دانش‌آموز در معرض خطر مسمومیت","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-04-20","url":"https://fa.amnesty.org/schoolgirls-at-risk-of-poisoning/","claim":"Amnesty said that since November 2022 thousands of schoolgirls had been poisoned and hospitalized, and that authorities had failed to investigate and stop the attacks adequately.","locator":"opening summary of the Persian-language page","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Persian-language Amnesty page with a clear start date tied to late 2022 and an explicit investigative failure claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Starts in late 2022 and continues immediately afterward","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is to the Iranian state environment under Khamenei's rule, though the attacks themselves were not personally ordered in the source.","contrary_evidence":["The page is a 2023 publication, so it reflects early aftermath as well as the 2022 onset.","It documents suspected chemical attacks, not a completed criminal verdict."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}
- The UN fact-finding mission’s 2024 report is the strongest single synthesis of the protest repression pattern.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Report of the Independent International Fact-Finding Mission on the Islamic Republic of Iran","publisher":"United Nations Human Rights Council","publication_date":"2024-02-02","url":"https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/4039538/files/A_HRC_55_67-EN.pdf","claim":"The mission concluded that Iran bore state responsibility for Jina Mahsa Amini's unlawful death and found serious violations against protesters, including a pattern of force, detentions, internet restrictions, sexual and gender-based violence, and killings; it recorded 551 people killed by September 2023, including 49 women and 68 children.","locator":"summary and pp. 2-4, 7, 15-16","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN investigative report with detailed methodology, state-responsibility findings, and quantified casualties.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Post-period synthesis of the 16 Sept 2022 protest wave","ruler_attribution":"Strong state-level attribution under Khamenei's authority, though the report is not a personal command transcript.","contrary_evidence":["The report is post-period and summarizes a year-long investigation rather than day-by-day 2022 contemporaneous reporting.","It does not isolate every action to Khamenei personally."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.4","3B.5","3B.7","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
- A late-2022 official signal suggested the morality police might have been shut down, but the reporting made clear that the status was uncertain and the hijab regime remained.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran protesters call for strike, prosecutor says morality police shut down","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2022-12-04","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/iran-protesters-call-strike-prosecutor-121805969.html","claim":"Iran's public prosecutor said the morality police had been shut down, but there was no confirmation from the Interior Ministry and officials reiterated that the mandatory hijab policy would remain unchanged.","locator":"article body paragraphs on the prosecutor's statement and lack of confirmation","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire on an official statement, but the substance was immediately contested and the institutional status remained unclear.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Late 2022 and directly tied to the protest backlash","ruler_attribution":"Official-but-indirect state statement, not a direct Khamenei order.","contrary_evidence":["The report itself says the closure was unconfirmed.","It did not amount to an end of the coercive hijab regime."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.7","3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across Reuters syndications, OHCHR press releases and special-procedure communications, UN Human Rights Council material, the UN fact-finding mission report, Amnesty International reports in English and Persian, Human Rights Watch English and Persian country coverage, NetBlocks telemetry, Access Now shutdown reporting, and a few secondary explainers on the morality police.

I rejected or deprioritized:
- Duplicate Reuters syndications that repeated the same speech or incident without adding new facts.
- Purely derivative explainers that added no better claim or locator than the primary/near-primary source already retained.
- Out-of-period retrospectives unless they materially summarized the 2022 record or directly described late-2022 consequences.
- Lower-quality advocacy pages that repeated already-retained facts without a distinct material claim.
- Sources about international or nuclear conduct that belonged in Chapters 1B/2B rather than 3B.
- A few blocked or weakly accessible items where the accessible snippet was too thin to support a clean source-claim unit.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct official Persian transcripts from Khamenei’s office on the protest crackdown would improve ruler attribution, especially for 3B.3 and 3B.8.
- Better chain-of-command evidence linking specific lethal acts, detentions, and internet controls to Khamenei personally, rather than to the state apparatus generally, would sharpen attribution.
- The school-poisoning issue would benefit from a stronger 2022 primary or forensic source on perpetrators and command responsibility.
- The claim that the morality police were “shut down” remains ambiguous and would benefit from a direct authoritative confirmation or clear retraction.
- More granular victim-count data for individual provinces would help if you want a tighter severity map, but it is not necessary to establish the overall pattern of severe, recurring repression.
